{"id":"p06-l02","minutes":35,"summary":"Many microcontrollers have no floating-point unit, so control code uses fixed-point integers. You derive the Q15 format, multiply with rounding and saturation, and prove the error stays within half an LSB, matching a float reference over thousands of random products.","html":"<h2 id=\"q-formats\">Q formats</h2>\n<p>A <strong>Qm.n</strong> number is an integer that you agree to divide by <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6644em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6644em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">n</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>. <strong>Q15</strong> is a 16-bit signed integer read as <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.0641em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0315em;\">k</span><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">15</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>, covering <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">[</span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.0641em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">−</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">15</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\">]</span></span></span></span> in steps of <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">−</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">15</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≈</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">3.05</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">0</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">−</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">5</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>. <strong>Q31</strong> uses 32 bits for extra precision. Q15 suits filter coefficients and normalised signals; for physical values you pick <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span></span></span></span> to fit the range (a Q7.8 value in a 16-bit register covers ±128 in steps of 1/256).</p>\n<p><strong>Addition</strong> is ordinary integer addition, because both operands share the same scale. The result can overflow, so DSP code uses <strong>saturation</strong>: clamp to the largest or smallest representable value instead of wrapping around. In a control loop, a wrapped value turns full positive torque into full negative torque.</p>\n<p><strong>Multiplication</strong> doubles the scale: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.0641em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">a</span><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">15</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">b</span><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">15</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.0641em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">ab</span><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">30</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>. Keep the 32-bit product, then shift right by 15 to get back to Q15. Two details matter:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Rounding</strong>: add <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">14</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> before the shift. Plain truncation (shifting) always rounds toward −∞, which biases results by −½ LSB on average. That bias accumulates in integrators.</li>\n<li><strong>The one overflow case</strong>: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">+</span><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span>, which Q15 can’t represent. Saturate it to <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">−</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">15</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> (0x7FFF).</li>\n</ul>\n<p>With rounding, the error of each multiply is at most ½ LSB, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">−</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">16</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>.</p>\n\n<figure class=\"fig\"><div class=\"fig-body\"><div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"q15\" data-args=\"{}\"></div></div><figcaption>Error of 20 000 random Q15 multiplies against exact arithmetic. Rounding keeps the error centred within ±½ LSB; truncation shifts it to between −1 and 0.</figcaption></figure>\n<h2 id=\"worked-example\">Worked example</h2>\n<p>Multiply <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.7</span></span></span></span> by <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\">0.3</span></span></span></span> in Q15.</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Encode: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.7</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">32768</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">22</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">937.6</span></span></span></span>, round to 22 938. <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\">0.3</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">32768</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\">9830.4</span></span></span></span>, round to −9830.</li>\n<li>Integer product: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">22</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">938</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\">9830</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\">225</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">480</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">540</span></span></span></span>.</li>\n<li>Add <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">14</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">16</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">384</span></span></span></span> and shift right by 15 (floor division): <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">⌊</span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\">225</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">464</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">156/32768</span><span class=\"mclose\">⌋</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\">6881</span></span></span></span>.</li>\n<li>Decode: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\">6881/32768</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\">0.209991</span></span></span></span>. The exact product is −0.21; the error (+0.28 LSB) mostly comes from encoding 0.7 and −0.3, not from the multiply.</li>\n<li>Truncating instead gives <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">⌊</span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\">225</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">480</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">540/32768</span><span class=\"mclose\">⌋</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\">6882</span></span></span></span>, which is half an LSB further away.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"code-it-from-scratch\">Code it from scratch</h2>\n\n<div class=\"code-card\" data-code=\"0\"><div class=\"code-head\"><span class=\"fname\" translate=\"no\">q15.py</span><button class=\"btn btn-quiet btn-small\" type=\"button\" data-copy=\"0\">Copy</button><button class=\"btn btn-quiet btn-small\" type=\"button\" data-download=\"0\">Download</button></div><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code class=\"language-python\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">import</span> numpy <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">as</span> np\n\nONE = <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span> &lt;&lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">15</span>\nMAX, MIN = ONE - <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>, -ONE\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">sat</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">x</span>):\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">max</span>(MIN, <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">min</span>(MAX, x))\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">to_q15</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">x</span>):\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> sat(<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">int</span>(<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">round</span>(x * ONE)))\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">q15_add</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">a, b</span>):\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> sat(a + b)\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">q15_mul</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">a, b, rounding=<span class=\"hljs-literal\">True</span></span>):\n    p = a * b\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> sat((p + (<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span> &lt;&lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">14</span>)) &gt;&gt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">15</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> rounding <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">else</span> p &gt;&gt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">15</span>)   <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># &gt;&gt; is floor division, like the hardware</span>\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> __name__ == <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;__main__&quot;</span>:\n    a, b = to_q15(<span class=\"hljs-number\">0.7</span>), to_q15(-<span class=\"hljs-number\">0.3</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> (a, b) == (<span class=\"hljs-number\">22938</span>, -<span class=\"hljs-number\">9830</span>) <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">and</span> q15_mul(a, b) == -<span class=\"hljs-number\">6881</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">and</span> q15_mul(a, b, <span class=\"hljs-literal\">False</span>) == -<span class=\"hljs-number\">6882</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> q15_mul(MIN, MIN) == MAX                                 <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># -1 * -1 saturates</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> q15_add(to_q15(<span class=\"hljs-number\">0.75</span>), to_q15(<span class=\"hljs-number\">0.75</span>)) == MAX               <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># saturates instead of wrapping</span>\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(<span class=\"hljs-number\">15</span>)\n    A = rng.integers(MIN, MAX + <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">50_000</span>); B = rng.integers(MIN, MAX + <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">50_000</span>)\n    err_r = np.array([q15_mul(<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">int</span>(x), <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">int</span>(y)) <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> x, y <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">zip</span>(A, B)]) - A * B / ONE\n    err_t = np.array([q15_mul(<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">int</span>(x), <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">int</span>(y), <span class=\"hljs-literal\">False</span>) <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> x, y <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">zip</span>(A, B)]) - A * B / ONE\n    ok = ~((A == MIN) &amp; (B == MIN))\n    <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">f&quot;rounding: max |err| <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{np.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(err_r[ok]).<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">max</span>():<span class=\"hljs-number\">.4</span>f}</span> LSB, mean <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{err_r.mean():+<span class=\"hljs-number\">.4</span>f}</span>; truncation mean <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{err_t.mean():+<span class=\"hljs-number\">.4</span>f}</span> LSB&quot;</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> np.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(err_r[ok]).<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">max</span>() &lt;= <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.5</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">and</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(err_r.mean()) &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.01</span>   <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># within half an LSB, unbiased</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> -<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span> &lt; err_t.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">min</span>() <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">and</span> err_t.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">max</span>() &lt;= <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">and</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(err_t.mean() + <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.5</span>) &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.01</span></code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"exercises\">Exercises</h2>\n\n<div class=\"exercise\"><div class=\"ex-q\"><p>A motor current of ±40 A must be stored in a 16-bit signed register with the finest resolution possible. Which Q format, and what’s the resolution?</p>\n</div><details><summary>Show the solution</summary><div class=\"ex-s\"><p>You need ±40, so 6 integer bits plus sign cover ±64: Q6.9, giving <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1/512</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1.95</span></span></span></span> mA steps. (Q5.10 only reaches ±32.)</p>\n</div></details></div>\n\n<div class=\"exercise\"><div class=\"ex-q\"><p>Why does truncation make a discrete integrator drift?</p>\n</div><details><summary>Show the solution</summary><div class=\"ex-s\"><p>Each truncated multiply errs by −½ LSB on average. An integrator sums thousands of them, so the error grows linearly with time instead of averaging out.</p>\n</div></details></div>\n<h2 id=\"quiz\">Quiz</h2>\n\n<div class=\"quiz\" data-quiz=\"p06-l02\"></div>\n\n","toc":[{"id":"q-formats","title":"Q formats"},{"id":"worked-example","title":"Worked example"},{"id":"code-it-from-scratch","title":"Code it from scratch"},{"id":"exercises","title":"Exercises"},{"id":"quiz","title":"Quiz"}],"quiz":[{"id":"p06-l02-q1","type":"num","q":"<p>What is 0.7 in Q15 (rounded)?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Multiply by <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">15</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>.</p>\n","answer":22938,"tol":0.0001,"unit":""},{"id":"p06-l02-q2","type":"num","q":"<p>Q15 product of 22938 and −9830, with rounding?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Add <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">14</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>, then floor-shift by 15.</p>\n","answer":-6881,"tol":0.0001,"unit":""},{"id":"p06-l02-q3","type":"num","q":"<p>What is one Q15 LSB as a decimal?</p>\n","explain":"<p><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">−</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">15</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>.</p>\n","answer":0.000030518,"tol":0.001,"unit":""},{"id":"p06-l02-q4","type":"mc","q":"<p>Saturation means…</p>\n","explain":"<p>Wrapping flips the sign, which is dangerous in control.</p>\n","options":["rounding to the nearest LSB","converting to float","clamping to the largest or smallest representable value","wrapping around on overflow"],"answer":2},{"id":"p06-l02-q5","type":"mc","q":"<p>The only Q15 × Q15 product that overflows is…</p>\n","explain":"<p>+1 isn’t representable in Q15.</p>\n","options":["1 × 1","0.5 × 0.5","−1 × 1","−1 × −1"],"answer":3},{"id":"p06-l02-q6","type":"num","q":"<p>Resolution in mA of Q6.9 for amps?</p>\n","explain":"<p><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">−</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">9</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> A.</p>\n","answer":1.9531,"tol":0.001,"unit":"mA"}],"code":[{"file":"q15.py","lang":"python","src":"import numpy as np\n\nONE = 1 << 15\nMAX, MIN = ONE - 1, -ONE\n\ndef sat(x):\n    return max(MIN, min(MAX, x))\n\ndef to_q15(x):\n    return sat(int(round(x * ONE)))\n\ndef q15_add(a, b):\n    return sat(a + b)\n\ndef q15_mul(a, b, rounding=True):\n    p = a * b\n    return sat((p + (1 << 14)) >> 15 if rounding else p >> 15)   # >> is floor division, like the hardware\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    a, b = to_q15(0.7), to_q15(-0.3)\n    assert (a, b) == (22938, -9830) and q15_mul(a, b) == -6881 and q15_mul(a, b, False) == -6882\n    assert q15_mul(MIN, MIN) == MAX                                 # -1 * -1 saturates\n    assert q15_add(to_q15(0.75), to_q15(0.75)) == MAX               # saturates instead of wrapping\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(15)\n    A = rng.integers(MIN, MAX + 1, 50_000); B = rng.integers(MIN, MAX + 1, 50_000)\n    err_r = np.array([q15_mul(int(x), int(y)) for x, y in zip(A, B)]) - A * B / ONE\n    err_t = np.array([q15_mul(int(x), int(y), False) for x, y in zip(A, B)]) - A * B / ONE\n    ok = ~((A == MIN) & (B == MIN))\n    print(f\"rounding: max |err| {np.abs(err_r[ok]).max():.4f} LSB, mean {err_r.mean():+.4f}; truncation mean {err_t.mean():+.4f} LSB\")\n    assert np.abs(err_r[ok]).max() <= 0.5 and abs(err_r.mean()) < 0.01   # within half an LSB, unbiased\n    assert -1 < err_t.min() and err_t.max() <= 0 and abs(err_t.mean() + 0.5) < 0.01"}]}